    {
      "title": "India Post revenue crosses ₹4,000 cr for second straight quarter: Scindia",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/india-post-revenue-crosses-4-000-cr-for-second-straight-quarter-scindia-126102200613_1.html",
      "description": "The Department of Posts (DoP) has breached the Rs 4,000 crore revenue mark in two successive quarters for the first time, Union Communications Minister Jyotiraditya Scindia said on Thursday.\nDoP, which operates the India Post brand, clocked 25 per cent growth to Rs 4,202 crore in the second quarter ended September 30, 2026 compared to Rs 3,355 crore a year ago, Scindia said.\n\"We achieved a revenue of Rs 4,202 crore for the second quarter, an almost 5 per cent increase (quarter-on-quarter). This is the first time in the history of India Post that we have breached the Rs 4,000 crore mark for two successive quarters,\" the minister said.\nThe growth was led by Parcel, which was up 71 per cent. Postal Life Insurance (PLI) and Rural PLI grew 44 per cent compared to September 2025 quarter. The International Business (IB) grew 38 per cent.\n\"Now, keeping this in mind, our H1 (first half) revenue has grown by almost 24 per cent compared to H1 of last year. Last year's H1 was roughly about Rs",
